Proposed fix — NOT APPLIED (leaf seat). Target: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kama-shokunin/tools/append-only-audit.py lines 165-172
Reason: git quotes a pathname containing "unusual" characters in --numstat output unless -z is used
(diff-format page, rendered lines 2057-2060; git-diff page, rendered lines 3500-3512). The tool keys
the per-file deletion count on the tab-split third field, so such a path would never match the
contract path and its deletions would be silently unaudited. With --no-renames every record is a
single-path record, so a -z triplet parse is exact.
Residual limit even after this change: _text() decodes with errors="replace", so bytes that are not
valid UTF-8 in a pathname would still not round-trip; a bytes-based key would be needed for those.
The identical parse in the frozen counter (tools/round47-append-audit-v2-check.py:189-198) is out of
scope for a fix — the counter is frozen; this report records it as a finding.

--- a/tools/append-only-audit.py
+++ b/tools/append-only-audit.py
@@ -165,10 +165,11 @@
 def numstat(repo, parent, commit, files):
     res = {}
-    raw = _text(repo, "diff", "--numstat", "--no-renames", parent, commit, "--", *files)
-    for line in raw.split("\n"):
-        parts = line.split("\t")
-        if len(parts) >= 3 and parts[1].isdigit():
-            res[parts[2]] = int(parts[1])
+    raw = _text(repo, "diff", "--numstat", "--no-renames", "-z", parent, commit, "--", *files)
+    fields = raw.split("\0")
+    for i in range(0, len(fields) - 2, 3):
+        deleted, path = fields[i + 1], fields[i + 2]
+        if deleted.isdigit():
+            res[path] = int(deleted)
     return res
